    "finalText": "Done — the URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified (36/36 smoke checks passed).\n\n**What I built** (Express 4.21.2 pinned, Node 22, Knex + `pg` as the idiomatic relational layer with migrations):\n\n- `src/app.js` — all routes: `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, URL echoed unchanged, generated 8-char codes from a 64-char alphabet, duplicate custom code → 409), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` increment), and `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`)\n- Validation → 422 for malformed JSON, missing/invalid url (non-absolute, non-http(s), no host), and invalid codes (must match 4–20 of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`); all errors are JSON `{error: ...}`\n- `knexfile.js` + `migrations/` — DB settings read only from `DATABASE_URL`\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n\n**Verified**: every functional rule, edge-length codes (4 and 20 chars), duplicate 409, all 422 paths, unknown-code 404s, exact once-per-request click increments, raw non-ASCII URLs (Location header fallback), and restart persistence — links, click counts, and creation order all survived a full stop/start, with migrations idempotent on second run. I cleaned my test rows out of the database and stopped my server so port 8000 is free for the graded run."
